{
  "summary": "Call with Maya (them), with Yossi (operations) joining on shipping questions. The client is a chain of 14 container stores that wants online ordering with delivery time windows; today orders come by phone and a shared spreadsheet. The launch target is before the holidays, and they must go live within four weeks. Management approved a budget of about 45,000 ש\"ח for the whole project. The catalog has about 4,000 SKUs, with roughly a third (about 1,300) online at launch. Open questions: whether we can connect to their inventory system (an old system on a local server, its vendor closed; Yossi will send the manual by email today); how delivery windows should work (two-hour windows, with a per-store cap per window); whether we handle storage and maintenance after launch (we have a package, to be detailed in the proposal); whether Ilan, the decision maker, can join the next call; and whether we handle pickup lockers in stores. Maya received a competing quote from a larger firm at about half our price and is worried about it; we agreed to compare it line by line. Payments go through a payment provider, so card details never touch their server. A loyalty app was raised and deferred. Yossi will send the delivery zone file after the call. Dan promised a sample proposal.",
  "resolve": [],
  "update": [
    {"id": "q3", "fields": {"text": "me to them: אילן יוכל להצטרף לשיחה הבאה? (תשובה: אולי)"}}
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "Dan (me) is evaluating a hosting provider; Sam and Priya (solutions engineer) are on the call. Dan expects about 40,000 visits a month. His current setup is a single virtual server with two CPUs and nightly backups. Dan needs at least 99.95% uptime. Sam said that requires the business tier, which has different SLA credits. The business tier costs $520 per month, above Dan's $400 budget. Sam said a discount may be possible on an annual commitment; Dan asked for a three-month start and Sam will check with Sam's team about a smaller trial plan. Priya confirmed Frankfurt data center has space. Migration is typically under an hour of downtime, done at night. Sam said the $300 setup fee is waived for annual customers, after first describing migration as free with a $300 setup fee. Dan does not need an RPO beyond a day; nightly backups are acceptable for now. Sam will send the SLA and migration plan by Tuesday, plus the migration checklist file. Open: backup retention period and whether a single site can be restored; support response time to be put in writing in the SLA; whether the price can come down. A CDN add-on was parked by Dan.",
  "resolve": ["q1", "q4", "q6", "q5"],
  "update": [
    {"id": "c1", "fields": {"text": "them: Priya will send the migration information and the SLA by Tuesday [open]"}},
    {"id": "c2", "fields": {"text": "them: Send the migration checklist file with the SLA [open]"}},
    {"id": "o2", "fields": {"text": "me: Asked whether migration is free or there is a $300 setup fee; told the fee is waived for annual customers [resolved in call]"}}
  ]
}
